# f1 = count, f2 = shown, f3 = sum
# A key made by `+` out of fields of rows that nobody has typed stayed `Add form=Generic`: a rope, which every access under it turned into a name anew (about 1,000 instructions a row). Where one addend
# is a proven text and the other is a number, a text, a boolean, undefined or null, the sum is the text of the other joined to it and runs no code: the other is asked for that and goes into a likely
# name as it is (a number is not made a string first); whatever else it is takes the sum as it was, on a rare way. A join that nobody reads as a key stays as it was, and so does a sum of two values
# of which neither is a text: it may be a number.
# RUN: walk f1:Body mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: PropGet {{*}} key="region"
# CHECK: TypeTest {{*}} testedType=undefined|null|boolean|number|string
# CHECK: Strcat {{*}} [isLikelyKey, isLikelyName]
# CHECK: frequency=Rare
# CHECK: Add {{*}} form=Generic
# CHECK: PropGet {{*}} key="kind"
# CHECK: TypeTest {{*}} testedType=undefined|null|boolean|number|string
# CHECK: Strcat {{*}} [isLikelyKey, isLikelyName]
# CHECK: frequency=Rare
# CHECK: Add {{*}} form=Generic
# CHECK: ElemGet
# RUN(NONE): walk f1:Body mechanisms=all
# NONE-NOT: form=MayBeString
# RUN(SHOWN): walk f2:Body mechanisms=all
# SHOWN-LABEL: code f2:Body
# SHOWN-NOT: isLikelyKey
# SHOWN: Add {{*}} form=Generic
# SHOWN-NOT: isLikelyKey
# RUN(SUM): walk f3:Body mechanisms=all
# SUM-LABEL: code f3:Body
# SUM-NOT: Strcat
# SUM: Add {{*}} form=Generic
# SUM-NOT: Strcat
